---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { AlertVariants, AlertActions, AlertContent, AlertStates } from '../../components/AlertDemo';
---

<Docs title="Alert" description="Inline messages for errors, warnings, and status that stay on the page.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Alert</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    An inline message that stays in place. Use it for errors, conflicts, and notes next to the content they affect.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="alert-demo">
    <AlertVariants client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Alert usage"
      code={`import {
  Alert,
  AlertAction,
  AlertDescription,
  AlertTitle,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/alert";
import { InfoCircle } from "reicon-react/icons/InfoCircle";

<Alert variant="destructive">
  <AlertTitle>This table is unavailable</AlertTitle>
  <AlertDescription>
    It was deleted, or your access to it changed.
  </AlertDescription>
</Alert>

<Alert role="status">
  <InfoCircle aria-hidden="true" />
  <AlertTitle>Chat archived</AlertTitle>
  <AlertDescription>It moved to Archived chats.</AlertDescription>
  <AlertAction>
    <Button variant="ghost" size="sm" onClick={undo}>Undo</Button>
  </AlertAction>
</Alert>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>variant</code> is <code>"default"</code> or <code>"destructive"</code>. Both sit on the surface color.
      Destructive tints the text, title, and icon with <code>--sprout-danger</code>. There is one size.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every part is optional. Use a description alone for short notes, add a title for a headline, and put an icon first
      to get a two-column layout. Icons are sized to 16px unless they carry a <code>size-*</code> class.{' '}
      <code>AlertAction</code> pins a small control to the top-right corner and reserves space for it.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Actions</h2>
    <p>
      Put recovery buttons after the description in a wrapping row, or place a single button as a direct child. Direct
      buttons and buttons inside the description align to the start instead of stretching. A link-style button in the
      description stays inline with the text.
    </p>
    <AlertActions client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Rich content</h2>
    <p>
      Descriptions accept paragraphs, lists, and links. Paragraphs are spaced for you; lists keep the classes you give
      them. Plain text, <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> work as direct children too. The content
      column can shrink to zero, so long names wrap instead of overflowing.
    </p>
    <AlertContent client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      Alerts are static. Your app decides when to show one and which variant to use. Switch <code>variant</code> from
      the outcome of the work, and render one alert per item when several things fail.
    </p>
    <AlertStates client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="alert-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Alert render"
      code={`import { Alert, alertVariants } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/alert";

<Alert role="note" render={<section />}>…</Alert>

<div role="alert" className={alertVariants({ variant: "destructive" })}>
  {error}
</div>`}
    />
    <p>
      All four parts render a <code>div</code> and accept the Base UI <code>render</code> prop, <code>className</code>,{' '}
      <code>ref</code>, and any HTML attribute. <code>alertVariants()</code> returns the alert classes for elements you
      render yourself.
    </p>
    <p>
      Parts get <code>data-slot</code> values of <code>alert</code>, <code>alert-title</code>,{' '}
      <code>alert-description</code>, and <code>alert-action</code>. The root also gets <code>data-variant</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Alert</code> has <code>role="alert"</code> by default, so screen readers announce it when it appears. Pass{' '}
      <code>role="status"</code> for results that should not interrupt, or <code>role="note"</code> for standing
      information. Mark icons <code>aria-hidden</code>; the words carry the meaning.
    </p>
    <p>
      Alerts never take focus. Buttons and links inside keep their own focus rings and keyboard behavior. Alerts fade in
      over 180ms; links change color over 120ms. Both stop when reduced motion is requested.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Alerts use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-text</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>, <code>--sprout-danger</code>, and <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>. They follow
      light and dark mode and need no brand color, so they look the same with the neutral and TulipFarm themes.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
